    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="40570bc0-fdf8-5b4a-9299-1542e649a890" activityNameId="de8a7958-9fea-5a93-956c-714caa5e4045" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Wood chips, from industry, softwood, burned in furnace 1000kW</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Wood chips, from industry, softwood, burned in furnace 1000kW
Heat of combustion of wood chips based on lower heating value. 2100 operating hours per year. Air emission factors are calculated from the weighted average of measurements of automatic chip boilers &gt; 500 kW.;
UUID: 71493667-796e-36d7-99b8-2c87bcbf25cf
This module describes the combustion of wood chips. Included are the infrastructure, the wood requirements, the emissions to air, the transport of the fuel, the electricity needed for operation, and the disposal of the ashes.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Boiler of average technology available on market
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_71493667-796e-36d7-99b8-2c87bcbf25cf.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
